%------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% gmat_translunar.script -- frozen-truth generation run for the Phase 8
% trans-lunar cross-tool case (exit criterion 1, D-15). Replicates the
% BALLISTIC COAST of missions/tli.toml in GMAT R2026a. Full replication
% specification: tests/golden/crosstool/README.md; provenance and command
% line: manifest.toml.
%
% Why the coast, not the burn. The gate is "trans-lunar < 1 km at lunar
% arrival": it measures the transfer TRAJECTORY, not the finite TLI burn. The
% burn (prograde_hold) is a simulator-internal maneuver; the cross-tool
% comparison propagates both tools ballistically from the simulator's exact
% post-burn ballistic state and compares position where the coast enters the
% Moon's sphere of influence. This isolates the coast dynamics both tools
% model identically and removes the finite-burn replication as a source of
% tool difference. The simulator side of the comparison is the tli truth log
% sampled from t = 354 s (ballistic burnout) onward.
%
% Burnout is t = 354 s, NOT the meco event time 353 s. The cutoff is COMMANDED
% at the meco timer (t = 353 s), but the delivered thrust level follows the
% per-step spool discipline (docs/mathlib propulsion chapter, PROP-SPOOL-RAMP)
% on the mission's 1 s integrator grid: the [353, 354) step still integrates
% at the pre-command level and the level is exactly zero from t = 354 s.
% Measured in the truth log: specific orbital energy gains a full-thrust step
% over [353, 354) (+15.3 m/s equivalent prograde delta-v) and is constant from
% 354 s on. The first freeze of this case used the t = 353 s state and was
% invalidated: the 15.3 m/s energy deficit amplifies through the near-capture
% lunar approach into a 75,189 km matched-epoch arrival miss (the failing gate
% printed 75,212 km because the superseded test additionally sampled the
% simulator log at the CSV's elapsed stamp without the 353 s offset -- a
% comparison-epoch misalignment worth ~45 km on its own, fixed by the explicit
% epoch mapping the corrected test asserts). The simulator's own ballistic
% coast of that same mid-burn state reproduced the invalidated GMAT arrival
% state to 0.022 km, which is what localized the disagreement to the initial
% state, not the tools.
%
% Controlled-comparison configuration (documented in the manifest):
%   * Central body Earth, EarthICRF (the mission's Earth-centred GCRF).
%   * Force model: Earth point mass plus the Sun and Luna as point masses (the
%     mission's central_body = "earth" with a point-mass Earth - no gravity
%     table - and third_bodies = ["sun", "moon"]). No SRP, no drag: tli.toml
%     configures none.
%   * DE440 point-mass source: the DE-file set the zero-EOP startup file
%     selects, the same DE440 family as the committed excerpt tli.toml reads.
%   * EOP: run with --startup_file gmat_startup_zeroeop.txt (as the other
%     Earth-regime cases), though at cislunar distances the Earth-orientation
%     convention is immaterial to the < 1 km gate.
%   * Fixed-step integration (ErrorControl = None, 60 s RK89 steps). The coast
%     is 455755 - 354 = 455401 s; 455401 is not a multiple of 60, so the
%     comparison samples the trajectory at the SOI-arrival epoch located by
%     the simulator (the manifest records the arrival epoch and the compared
%     state).
%   * Burnout Cartesian state (EarthICRF), the simulator's exact tli t = 354 s
%     truth state (the first ballistic epoch, see above), so both tools start
%     from identical numbers. Epoch is the tli burnout epoch
%     2025-12-28T12:05:54Z (t0 2025-12-28T12:00:00Z + 354 s).
%
% This script contains maintainer-machine absolute paths by design: D-15 runs
% the external tools offline on the maintainer machine only; CI never runs it.
%------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Create Spacecraft sat;
GMAT sat.DateFormat = UTCGregorian;
GMAT sat.Epoch = '28 Dec 2025 12:05:54.000';
GMAT sat.CoordinateSystem = EarthICRF;
GMAT sat.DisplayStateType = Cartesian;
GMAT sat.X = 2935.113038034428;
GMAT sat.Y = -5362.330919384242;
GMAT sat.Z = -2782.6716981243067;
GMAT sat.VX = 10.226771053695357;
GMAT sat.VY = 2.9192276112691835;
GMAT sat.VZ = 1.9036603302281139;
GMAT sat.DryMass = 1000;

Create ForceModel fm;
GMAT fm.CentralBody = Earth;
GMAT fm.PointMasses = {Earth, Sun, Luna};
GMAT fm.Drag = None;
GMAT fm.SRP = Off;
GMAT fm.RelativisticCorrection = Off;
GMAT fm.ErrorControl = None;

Create Propagator prop;
GMAT prop.FM = fm;
GMAT prop.Type = RungeKutta89;
GMAT prop.InitialStepSize = 60;
GMAT prop.MinStep = 0.001;
GMAT prop.MaxStep = 60;
GMAT prop.MaxStepAttempts = 50;

Create ReportFile rpt;
GMAT rpt.Filename = 'C:/Users/hoyer/WorkSpace/tools/crosstool-runs/gmat_translunar_report.txt';
GMAT rpt.Precision = 16;
GMAT rpt.WriteHeaders = true;
GMAT rpt.LeftJustify = On;
GMAT rpt.FixedWidth = true;
GMAT rpt.WriteReport = true;
GMAT rpt.Add = {sat.ElapsedSecs, sat.UTCModJulian, sat.EarthICRF.X, sat.EarthICRF.Y, sat.EarthICRF.Z, sat.EarthICRF.VX, sat.EarthICRF.VY, sat.EarthICRF.VZ};

BeginMissionSequence;

% Coast from ballistic burnout through lunar arrival. The stop time is the
% simulator's SOI-transition elapsed-from-burnout span (455755 - 354 =
% 455401 s); the manifest records the arrival-epoch state used for the < 1 km
% comparison.
Propagate prop(sat) {sat.ElapsedSecs = 455401.0};
